    {
      "id": "s9zskbl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "056vn3u",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2jub7v7",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "e5ufy69",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3jt9ijf",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jmbzgj0",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kbg6dro",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "80ezevx",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "kos1b6w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tvy8nbm",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xpgcve7",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ammeters have very low resistance and must be connected in series; Voltmeters have very high resistance and must be connected in parallel.",
        "Fuse wires are made of an alloy with a low melting point and high resistance, always connected in series with the live wire.",
        "1 kWh (Kilowatt-hour) is the commercial unit of electrical energy, equal to 3.6 × 10^6 Joules."
      ],
      "id": "lyrjhmw"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xmh25e3",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "niq1t78",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z6s9fnt",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "qd8cp70",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4oeykb",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5557wtx",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "klzy9go",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kuv56r8",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}